---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <section class="about-container">
    <div class="about-image">
      <img src="/images/profile.jpg" alt="Melanie Song portrait" />
    </div>

    <div class="about-text">
    
      <h1 class="about-title">Hello Again!</h1>

      <p>
        I've always been someone who <strong>makes things</strong>. Growing up, that looked like sketchbooks and studio art classes. Later, it became spreadsheets and business models. Now, it's <strong>UX research and product design</strong> — and honestly, it feels like the place where all of it finally fits together. Before I found design, I spent years in <strong>finance and business analysis</strong> — roles where I learned to think in data, systems, and trade-offs. What I kept noticing, though, was that the <strong>human side of decisions</strong> often got lost. That's what pulled me toward UX.
      </p>

      <p>
        Now, as a Master's student in <strong>Human-Centered Design & Engineering at University of Washington</strong>, I bring both sides to the table: the <strong>analytical rigor</strong> of someone who's lived in spreadsheets, and the <strong>empathy</strong> of someone who genuinely wants to understand what frustrates people and why. I care most about <strong>research-driven design</strong> — finding the insight that reframes the whole problem.
      </p>

      <p>
        When I'm not designing, I'm cooking something new, doing puzzles, or drawing. My mini goldendoodle supervises all of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
